    "distinct_from_closed_families": [
      "The closed prior-200-day DRA long-trend admission compares close with a long simple average; DMI uses adjacent-day competing extrema movement normalized by smoothed true range.",
      "The closed RSI, MACD and monthly momentum rules derive direction from closes; DMI derives direction from high and low expansion and separately smooths unsigned directional strength.",
      "The closed Supertrend rule uses an ATR-scaled ratcheted price band; DMI has no price band, crossing stop or trailing stop.",
      "The closed Donchian rule uses fixed prior extrema breakouts; DMI uses adjacent-day directional movement before smoothing.",
      "The closed OBV rule uses signed volume; DMI uses no volume."
    ],
    "excluded_reinterpretations": [
      "DMI14 and ADX14 strictly above 25 is the primary policy. ADX thresholds 20 and 30 are rejection-only neighbors and cannot replace a failed primary.",
      "No alternate DI or ADX length, threshold, smoothing, initialization, price basis, crossover-only rule, stop, trailing stop, confirmation, delay, minimum hold, cash yield, leverage, short leg, DRA interaction or ensemble may be scanned after outcome access.",
      "A historical pass remains REPORTED_NOT_ACTIVATED and requires at most one independent sealed OOS."
    ]
